{
 "result": "maze.py is a padded-bytearray BFS: it reads the grid from stdin, pads it with '#' so neighbour checks need no bounds tests, marks visited cells by overwriting them with '#', and expands frontier by level, printing the distance at E or -1. It passes all three public samples (2008, -1, 78) and the assay is registered as baseline 3.96644 (noise 6.4%). I stopped here rather than spend energy on variants: the body is already a straightforward linear-time BFS, and a win needs more than 6.4% over baseline, which I did not have a clear candidate for.",
